        <definition>float AGE::Timer::Elapsed</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>Elapsed</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGE::Timer::Elapsed</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function returns the elapsed time in milliseconds since the start time &apos;m_Start&apos;. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The function uses std::chrono to measure the duration between the current time and the start time. It then converts this duration from nanoseconds to milliseconds by dividing by 1,000,000 (since there are 1,000,000 nanoseconds in a millisecond). The result is returned as a float.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>A float representing the elapsed time in milliseconds.</para>
</simplesect>
This function returns the elapsed time in milliseconds since the start time &apos;m_Start&apos;.</para>
<para>The function uses a high resolution clock to measure the elapsed time and then converts it into milliseconds. It does this by first converting the duration into nanoseconds, then dividing by 1 million (to convert from nanoseconds to microseconds) and finally again by 1000 (to convert from microseconds to milliseconds). The result is a float representing the elapsed time in milliseconds.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>A float representing the elapsed time in milliseconds since &apos;m_Start&apos;. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
